From 3c6d4d78127106aa38f0e3dfd8279adf1470d963 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Beany <24502088+beanyforever@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:04:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Writers outside the job queue read, change and save in a turn

Jobs hold flushLock while they read, change and save. Many writers outside
the job queue read a page or database, changed it and saved it without the
lock, so a job's save that landed between their read and their save was
written over with no error. Patch 0007's tripwire names them.

Eighteen entry points now take a turn of flushLock, as a job does:
- setBlockAttrs and batchSetBlockAttrs;
- getAttributeViewKeys, a writable renderAttributeView and
  getAttributeViewPrimaryKeyValues. They read without a turn, and save a
  database only when they changed it, in a turn, and only if the database
  cache's version noted before their read still holds;
- page deletion, with patch 0003's check inside the turn, and renames;
- "+ New" and createAttributeViewItemDocs, with the content template;
- the ref-text job and the refresh after moveBlock, which read their
  definitions again in each short turn, and only those its refs name;
- transferBlockRef, duplicating a database block, page history, one-page
  snapshot and database history restores, daily notes, moving pages and
  asset rename.

takeTurn runs the jobs queued before it, as PerformTransactionSync does, and
isFlushing covers only those jobs, so FlushTxQueue doesn't wait out a
writer's turn. withTurn is its panic-safe form. turnMode serves functions
reached both inside and outside a turn, so nothing takes the turn twice.
Slow writers take a short turn per page or database. Work that waits for the
job queue (snapshots, mounting, index rebuilds, template rendering) runs
before the turn.

A one-page snapshot restore notes its target's version and backs up. In its
turn it restores only if the version still holds. Otherwise it gives the
file a second that no stored copy of it holds, backs up again, and waits for
the clock to pass that second, for up to three tries.

Still saving outside a turn: addAttributeViewKey, removeAttributeViewKey
and removeAttributeViewBlocks, the MCP database and file tools, the CLI and
the page tree's sort. Still open, as on v3.8.7: a restore's first backup
leaves out a save made in the second of the latest snapshot's copy of the
file, and a flashcard deck's restore writes over a save made after its
backup.

The tests, all through what SiYuan serves:
- a test per entry point in which a job saves between the writer's read and
  its save, each failing on v3.8.7 with patches 0001 to 0007;
- tests that the reads that save leave an unchanged database unsaved;
- deadlock guards for writers reached inside a job;
- a tripwire check that each writer saves within its turn;
- the review rounds' tests;
- TestTurnsStressJobsAndEveryWriter, a 30 s stress test that the image
  build leaves out.
