+// flushLock isn't reentrant, so a function that may already be in a turn (inside a job, or under a writer that took
+// one) never calls takeTurn: it has an in-turn variant, which takes nothing, and only the variant reached outside every
+// turn takes the turn. Nor does anything wait for the job queue while it has the turn (FlushTxQueue, WaitForCommit,
+// PerformTxSync, PerformTransactionSync, PerformTransactions followed by a wait): the queue runs only in turns, so it
+// would wait forever. A writer that needs both waits first and takes its turn after. The lock order stays flushLock,
+// then the encrypted-notebook operation, then hpathRefresh, then fileTreeSortLock: a writer takes its turn before them.
+func takeTurn() (release func()) {
