+// "+ New" in a database keeps a job's change to the page it made, made between "+ New"'s read of the page and its
+// next save of it. "+ New" makes the page, then loads it again to put the content template in and save it, then loads
+// it again to give it the template's attributes and save it; the editor opens the page meanwhile, where the owner can
+// type into it. polka's audit makes a row's page through createAttributeViewItemDocs, which saves the same way.
+func TestNewRowKeepsAJobsSaveToItsPageMadeBetweenItsReadAndItsSave(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Run("createAttributeViewItem, the template's attributes", func(t *testing.T) {
